                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Game is fine. Never played any others in this series. Art and animations are beautiful and fluid, so that's nice. It's fairly easy to pick up and play, and nothing felt too ridiculous except arguably a room or two in the final dungeon. It's occasionally funny in a wacky sort of way, and very imaginative in it's presentation. Gameplay isn't particularly imaginative though; it's not bad, but also not special. It's also quite an easy game, especially as a Metroidvania. What story there is is fairly lame, and sort of makes it feel like you're spinning your wheels. But again, overall, it's easy to play and charming, and I had enough enjoyment playing it over a few days while sick with the flu. I doubt I will ever play it again, however.",
